{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105510","id":2467042743,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6TDBW3","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105510","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105510.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105510.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105510","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105510/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105510/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105510/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/4af7bec432ce25ded8ff96a615f556955be3ff58","number":105510,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Implement audio absolute time (DSP time) and scheduled play","user":{"login":"PizzaLovers007","id":10912951,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwOTEyOTUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10912951?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007","html_url":"https://github.com/PizzaLovers007","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Note: This PR is superseded by #107226.**\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nImplementation is based off of @fire's notes 4 years ago: https://gist.github.com/fire/b9ed7853e7be24ab1d5355ef01f46bf1\r\n\r\nThe absolute time is calculated based on the total mixed frames and the mix rate. This means it only updates when a mix step happens.\r\n\r\nSpecific `play_scheduled` behaviors:\r\n- If a sound is playing, `play_scheduled()` will stop that sound (with single polyphony). This matches the behavior of play().\r\n- If a sound is scheduled, then paused, then resumed before the schedule happens, the sound still plays at the correct scheduled time.\r\n- If a playing sound is paused, then play_scheduled() is called, the sound will restart from the beginning. This matches the behavior of play().\r\n- With a higher `max_polyphony`, multiple sounds can be scheduled, and playing sounds can continue playing.\r\n- `play_scheduled` is unaffected by pitch scale.\r\n- `play_scheduled` does not support samples. The \"Stream\" default playback type is required for Web builds (ideally with threads enabled).\r\n\r\nScheduled stop is not implemented due to limited use cases.\r\n\r\n* Demo project: https://github.com/PizzaLovers007/play-scheduled-test\r\n* Web build: https://pizzalovers007.itch.io/godot-play-scheduled-demo?secret=l7sWHu1qrjbd5DQcEO1mpm4EQE\r\n\r\nFixes godotengine/godot-proposals#1151.\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch in priority.\r\n\r\nRelevant fixes are cherry-picked for stable branches as needed by maintainers.\r\n\r\nTo speed up the contribution process and avoid CI errors, please set up pre-commit hooks locally:\r\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/contributing/development/code_style_guidelines.html\r\n-->\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330068,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/feature%20proposal","name":"feature proposal","description":"","color":"4466ff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":